# any.map — logical name -> spec, shared across all package managers.
# Rows here are for provider-tagged (non-native) installs (§4). A per-distro map
# (apt.map, pacman.map, ...) overrides a row here when a distro differs.
#
# Format:  <logical name> = <spec>
#   spec with no method:   native package name(s), space-separated (one-to-many)
#   script:<url> [args]    pipe a remote installer to sh, args forwarded
#   source:<builder-fn>    build via a shell function in scope

# starship prompt is native on arch/alpine/void/gentoo + recent Debian/Ubuntu, so
# it passes through to the native package (updatable). Only the distros/releases
# that lack it carry a `script:` fallback row: dnf.map (Fedora) and apt.map
# (Ubuntu jammy/noble). Keeping it native-by-default honors §1's "no identity
# rows" — the exception is tagged, not the common case.

# wezterm is built from source on EVERY target (no AppImage, no flatpak): one
# recipe, one binary, everywhere. Upstream's ./get-deps installs the per-distro
# build deps, so this row needs no distro variants; the toolchain does not come
# for free, so list `rust` before `wezterm` in a rice (§4). Verified on Ubuntu
# (apt) — see test/unit/wezterm_module.sh + DESIGN §9.
wezterm = source:provide_wezterm

# yazi: upstream prebuilt binary (sxyazi/yazi releases), `cargo install` as the
# in-builder fallback. Installs both `yazi` and `ya` either way.
yazi = source:provide_yazi_bin

amneziavpn = source:provide_amneziavpn